Version 1.30
------------
Released 21-Mar-2023

- Parameter loading performance improvements, so BSI2010 and similar ECUs work in Diagnostique now
- Treeview no longer crashes when trying to load ECUs with high parameter count (see notes #1)
- Treeview has "Export Available Data" button, to generate a text file showing all available Actuator Tests, Live Data and Configuration options (+ states) for a specific ECU (#2)
- ECU headers loading improved, so there is now basic support for other protocols (FIAT_BCAN). However, this is not implemented in other places yet so Fiat-based systems don't work yet
- Additional error checking to various functions
- UDS keys are now included for many common ECUs, so secured telecoding will work for some ECUs now (note, traceability is not implemented yet)

#1 - The data load is now constrained to 80 000 database rows. This means data extraction is incomplete for BSI2010, VSM and other high parameter counts ECUs, but it will also not crash :) These ECUs, due to the way the database is currently managed, have over 1 million rows to a full data-set which is not manageable. This will be fixed in future

#2 - Only Configuration options which Diagnostique can show will be visible. Notably, this does not include parameters which have string or integer values as there is not yet support for these in the underling libraries


